f\n  \u2022 Pre-mortem triggers: housing recession (existing-home sales < 3.8M annualized), Section 232\n    expansion, energy spike > +25%.\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. Short thesis (same data):\n  1. You are paying 16.4x ADJUSTED FY26 EPS for a cyclical at mid-recovery, with Q1 FY27 guided margin\n     (6.5\u20137%) BELOW Q4 FY26 (7.1%) \u2014 margins are already rolling over [Actual].\n  2. Q4 adjusted operating income fell 20% YoY ($8.2M vs $10.3M) even as GAAP looked \"record\" \u2014 the\n     tariff refund (780bp) masks real operating deterioration [Actual].\n  3. Backlog down \u221211.8% sequentially; demand \"soft\"; consumer confidence weak; energy/Middle East\n     escalation [Actual \u2014 company].\n  4. The 24% buyback at $47 was funded with debt and spent the balance sheet; FY26 WC consumed $28M \u2014\n     the \"FCF machine\" may be a working-capital mirage [Arithmetic].\n  5. 12-year median operating margin is 5.5%; mean reversion to 6% would make the stock worth ~$70 \u2014\n     where ALL sell-side targets sit [Actual + Aggregator].\n  6. Thin coverage (1\u20132 analysts), 65.8% institutional ownership, 4.08M float \u2014 momentum unwinds are\n     violent when they start; short interest rising +21.9% MoM [Aggregator].\n  7. Without the one-time refund, FY26 adjusted EPS was already $4.94; at $80.93 you're paying for\n     9%+ margins, a margin level hit only once in the last 12 years [Arithmetic].\nStep 9-2. Logic combat: Long 6.5 / Short 7.5 \u2192 gap 1.0 < 2.0 \u219